    {
      "parameters": {
        "width": 496,
        "height": 1040,
        "content": "## Generate and Enrich Google Maps Leads with Apify, Google Sheets and Slack\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Starts manually or on the editable schedule and creates the delivery ledger if it is missing.\n2. Reads all user settings from the numbered configuration node and validates limits before any paid request.\n3. Runs `fetch_cat/google-maps-places-scraper` and `fetch_cat/website-contact-finder` through Cloud-compatible HTTP Request nodes and downloads at most 10 public results.\n4. Normalizes stable IDs and human-readable fields, skips states already delivered, uses deterministic rules without AI, and prepares one concise destination batch.\n5. Writes the selected results to Google Sheets, sends one Slack digest, then records item keys only after both destinations succeed. Failed deliveries remain retryable.\n\n### Setup\n\n- [ ] Add the Actor to Apify if required and create HTTP Header Auth with `Authorization: Bearer YOUR_APIFY_TOKEN`.\n- [ ] Select that credential in both Apify request nodes.\n- [ ] Connect Google Sheets and select the `Enriched leads` tab.\n- [ ] Connect Slack and choose the private QA destination.\n- [ ] Edit the numbered configuration node, run manually twice, and confirm the duplicate run sends nothing.\n- [ ] Publish the workflow only when you are ready to enable its schedule.\n\n### Customization\n\nChange the schedule, search inputs, threshold, result limit, destination, and digest wording without editing Code nodes. Keep live tests at 10 Actor items or fewer.",
        "color": 1
      },
